.TH blkdiscard 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
blkdiscard \- tell a device its blocks are no longer wanted
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blkdiscard
[\fB\-f\fR] \fIdevice\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blkdiscard
issues a discard, or TRIM, for the whole of
.IR device .
Flash media use it to know which blocks need not be preserved, which
helps their wear levelling and can make later writes faster.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-f
Do it without asking.
.SH NOTES
This destroys the contents of the device.  It is not an erase you can
undo, and it is not something to run on a device that holds anything you
want.
.PP
A device whose driver has no discard operation reports an error and
nothing happens.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkfs (1),
.BR fdisk (1)
